# Redirects for antisocialaudio.co.uk
#
# Sends addresses from the old WordPress site to the matching new page, so old links, bookmarks and
# Google results keep working. Cloudflare reads this file when the site is deployed.
#
# Format: one rule per line, "old-address  new-address  301". 301 means "moved for good", which tells
# Google to move the old page's ranking to the new one. Lines starting with # are notes.
#
# Rules of the file (Cloudflare docs: developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/):
# - Cloudflare treats /events and /events/ as different addresses, so each old page has two lines.
# - The new address can include a #section (e.g. /#prices); the browser jumps to it.
# - Query strings such as /?page_id=12 cannot be matched, so they are not listed.
# - Fixed addresses go first; the wildcard (*) rules go last. The first matching line wins.
# - Limits: 2,000 fixed and 100 wildcard rules.
#
# CONFIRMED old addresses (known from the current site):
#   /music-productibook-now/          the current booking page (Amelia)
#   /events/                          the current workshops page
#   /product/silkie-bassmasterclass/  the masterclass in the shop
#
# GUESSED old addresses: worked out from the old menu (Home, Packages, F.A.Q., Terms, DJ Bookings,
# Account, Book Lessons, Book Workshops) and the default addresses WordPress, WooCommerce and Yoast
# create. Before launch, check them against the WordPress export: in WordPress go to Pages > All Pages
# and Products > All Products (hover a title to see its address), or Tools > Export. Delete guesses
# that never existed and add any old address that is missing. A guess that never existed does no harm.
#
# Never point an old address at a page that does not exist on the new site.

